WEBVTT

00:16:59.681 --> 00:17:02.649
whether they were in the reversible
or irreversible condition.

00:17:02.673 --> 00:17:03.833
Wrong-o.

00:17:03.857 --> 00:17:05.026
Bad simulators.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:06.948
Because here's what's really happening.

00:17:06.972 --> 00:17:10.306
Both right before the swap
and five days later,

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:12.516
people who are stuck with that picture,

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:13.692
who have no choice,

00:17:13.716 --> 00:17:15.756
who can never change their mind,

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.209
like it a lot.

00:17:17.934 --> 00:17:20.885
And people who are deliberating --
"Should I return it?

00:17:20.909 --> 00:17:22.292
Have I gotten the right one?

00:17:22.316 --> 00:17:25.215
Maybe this isn't the good one.
Maybe I left the good one?" --

00:17:25.239 --> 00:17:26.439
have killed themselves.

00:17:26.463 --> 00:17:27.921
They don't like their picture.

00:17:27.945 --> 00:17:30.602
In fact, even after the opportunity
to swap has expired,